# Crontab alternative to the systemd timer for the v4 Weekly Audit Loop.
# Use this when systemd isn't available. Install with:  crontab ops/crontab.example
#
# The weekly cron is the ONLY scheduler the v4 design needs — the content-hash
# gate skips unchanged pages and carries their last report forward, so a weekly
# re-audit is cheap. The site-level Coverage Diff runs every week regardless,
# since missing pages have no hash to compare.
#
# Adjust paths, domain, and target. Load secrets/settings from the env file.

# Monday 03:00 — full audit cycle for the primary client. This ALSO auto-verifies the
# client's implementation milestones at the end of the loop (re-scrapes the live site and
# flips any task whose recommended page/offering/heading is now present to
# 'verified_completed', moving the dashboard's progress bar with no owner action).
0 3 * * 1  cd /opt/aeo && set -a && . /etc/aeo/audit.env && set +a && /opt/aeo/.venv/bin/aeo audit-cycle securin.io --target Securin >> /var/log/aeo/audit.log 2>&1

# Thursday 03:00 — lightweight mid-week milestone re-check (re-scrape + match only, no
# scoring/LLM), so a customer who shipped changes sees them verified without waiting for
# the next full audit. Drop this line if weekly verification (above) is enough.
0 3 * * 4  cd /opt/aeo && set -a && . /etc/aeo/audit.env && set +a && /opt/aeo/.venv/bin/aeo verify-milestones securin.io --target Securin >> /var/log/aeo/verify.log 2>&1
